            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "(haven't reviewed yet)\n\nIt would be great if someone could look into a fix for this so we could fix this properly.  Connecting SSL/Login to whether or not a UI is installed is a hack that would be nice to figure out how to break.\n\nWith that said, fixing this regression is probably fine as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Before the fix, hasWebuiRoute is inconsistent - between the point of setting it (e.g. webassets.hpp from webserver_run.cpp) and the point of getting it (i.e. ssl_key_handler.cpp.\n\nHere is the tracing.\n\n1)  Setting it as TRUE after startup\n```\nAug 08 13:29:22 p10bmc systemd[1]: Stopping Start bmcwebd server...\nAug 08 13:29:22 p10bmc systemd[1]: bmcweb.service: Deactivated successfully.\nAug 08 13:29:22 p10bmc systemd[1]: Stopped Start bmcwebd server.\nAug 08 13:29:24 p10bmc systemd[1]: Started Start bmcwebd server.\nAug 08 13:29:24 p10bmc bmcwebd[1089]: [webassets.hpp:220] TEST: webassets - addFile, SET hasWebuiRoute=true, as webpath=/\n```\n\n2) However, getting it as FALSE.\n```\nAug 08 13:29:24 p10bmc bmcwebd[1089]: [ssl_key_handler.cpp:551] TEST: getSslServerContext = c.tlsStrict=false, hasWebuiRoute = false\nAug 08 13:29:24 p10bmc bmcwebd[1089]: [ssl_key_handler.cpp:573] TEST: (forward_unauthorized::hasWebuiRoute==false) --- Setting verify peer only\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, I understand, that\u2019s a regression.  if the login/ssl connections were cleaned up to not require special casing for the webui, we wouldn\u2019t need this shared variable at all and this type of failure wouldn\u2019t be possible."
                }
            ],
